.TH BOSWAS-WELCOME 1 "October 2026" "boswas-branding 1.0~alpha3" "Boswas OS"
.SH NAME
boswas-welcome \- the Boswas OS terminal welcome
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B boswas-welcome
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints a short system summary: Boswas OS version, kernel, architecture,
session (live or installed), AppArmor state and device agent state, and
where to find more
.RB ( "boswas status" ,
.BR boswas-info ).
It reads local files only, so terminals open instantly.
.PP
The Boswas Konsole profiles start bash with
.IR /usr/share/boswas/terminal/bashrc ,
which runs the user's
.I ~/.bashrc
first, then sets the Boswas prompt and runs
.BR boswas-welcome .
Colour is used only on a terminal and is turned off by
.BR NO_COLOR .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/boswas/no-welcome
If it exists, Boswas terminals start without the welcome.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR boswas (1),
.BR boswas-preset (1)
